review_comment:
@eagleoflqj You are right. I tried to find an example of this to add a regression test, but could not find one. The result from `pure_complex` is only not `None` if it is of the form `a+b*i`, which `a` and `b` a `Number`. The only two options are a `Float` or a `Rational`, which both seem to work fine. Do you have an example?

Any subclass of `Number` has a field `_prec`, so we could even skip the checks on `m[i].is_Float`.

I updated the PR, but still have the checks on `is_Float` in place.

