review_comment:
The difference is pretty dramatic - for 1024 random symbols `Mul(*syms)` takes 0.025 seconds while `prod` takes 22.3. There is about a 10% slowdown for the int case if we do this:
```python
def prod(f, start=1):
    """return an int if all elements are ints else a SymPy expression"""
    from sympy.utilities.iterables import sift
    n, s = sift(f, lambda x: type(x) is int, binary=True)
    if start != 1:
        if type(start) is int:
            n.append(start)
	else:
	    s.append(start)
    if n:
        from math import prod as p
        return p(n) if not s else p(n)*Mul(*s)
    return Mul(*s)
```
But it seems better to me to just update internal uses of `prod` on ints to use `math.prod` and use `Mul(*factors)` or `sprod` (tba) for others and deprecate `mul.prod`.

