review_comment:
```py
import functools

class A:
    is_B = False
    a = 0

    @functools.cached_property
    def method(self):
        return isinstance(self, B)

class B(A):
    is_B = True
    a = 1
    b = 2

def f(a: A):
    print(a.a)
    if isinstance(a, B):
        print(a.b)
    if a.is_B:
        print(a.b)
    if a.method:
        print(a.b)

f(B())
```
```
hint.py:21: error: "A" has no attribute "b"
hint.py:23: error: "A" has no attribute "b"
```
This minimal example shows even using property mypy cannot tell a is B. I expect @overload could be used to decorate a field like is_Rational in future python version. Now `cast` has to be used to avoid `# type: ignore`.

