review_comment:
The PowerSet method should override this. It's not hard to implement the PowerSet.kind method:
```python
def kind(self):
    return SetKind(self.arg.kind)
```

```python
    @property
    def _kind(self):
        return SetKind(UndefinedKind)

    @property
    def _helper_kind(self):
        if not self.args:
            return SetKind()
        elif all(i.kind == self.args[0].kind for i in self.args):
            return SetKind(self.args[0].kind)
        else:
            return SetKind(UndefinedKind)

    @property
    def _union_setkind(self):
        args = tuple(arg.kind for arg in self.args if arg is not S.EmptySet)
        if not args:
            return SetKind()
        elif all(i == args[0] for i in args):
            return args[0]
        else:
            return SetKind(UndefinedKind)

    @property
    def _intersection_setkind(self):
        args = tuple(arg.kind for arg in self.args if arg is not S.UniversalSet)
        if not args:
            return SetKind(UndefinedKind)
        elif all(i == args[0] for i in args):
            return args[0]
        else:
            return SetKind()
```
Will this work?

I don't see why any of these are property methods. It would make more sense for a helper to be `classmethod`. 

The intersection method only seems to be used by the intersection class so it probably belongs there rather than as a helper.

The helper and union methods are basically the same so I think only one of them is needed. Probably just something like:
```
@classmethod
def _union_setkind(cls, kinds):
     kinds = set(kinds)
     if not kinds:
         return SetKind()
    elif if len(kinds) == 1:
         return SetKind(kinds.pop())
    else:
         return SetKind(UndefinedKind)
```
The FiniteSet can do
```
kinds = [e.kind for e in self.args]
return self._union_setkind(kinds)
```
And Union can do
```
kinds = [s.kind.element_kind for s in self.args if s is not S.EmptySet]
return self._union_setkind(kinds)
```
And Intersection can do
```
kinds = [s.kind.element_kind for s in self.args if s is not S.UniversalSet]
return self._union_setkind(kinds)
```

