Also, the failing docstring is a result of using `has` instead of the previous code. `f` is not an expression -- does not appear as any object's `arg` so the former code that only traversed args worked. The `has` walk is more general. If we want to use `has` then I need a way to identify the generators. With #22267 `has_free` is:
```python
def has_free(self, x):
    return x in generators(self)

def all_free(self, s):
    return not (generators(self) - s)
```
But then we really only need the `generators` since this is a pretty straightforward expression.

