review_comment:
I'm not sure if this is done automated or by hand, but if it is by hand, this code snippet might help:
```python
from sympy import (Abs, degree, expand, eye, floor, LC, Matrix, nan, Poly, pprint, QQ, pquo, quo, prem, rem, S, sign, simplify, summation, var, zeros)
imports={}
for obj in list(globals().values()):
    try:
        if 'sympy' in obj.__module__:
            try:
                imports[obj.__module__].append(obj.__name__)
            except:
                imports[obj.__module__]=[obj.__name__]       
    except:
        pass
for k,v in imports.items():
    print("from {0} import {1}".format(k,','.join(v)))
```
