review_comment:
The test intends to cover the *new-style* errback path in `_call_task_errbacks`, but `bind=True` makes the task’s `__header__` a `functools.partial` (see `head_from_fun(..., bound=True)`), so it won’t enter the new-style branch (`not isinstance(__header__, partial)` will be false). As a result, this test is likely exercising the old-style/group path and may pass even without the production fix. Consider defining `failing_errback` without `bind=True` (e.g., `def failing_errback(request, exc, traceback): ...`) so it is actually called via the new-style direct invocation and would have failed before this PR.
```suggestion
        @self.app.task(shared=False)
        def failing_errback(request, exc, traceback):
```

