`on_backend_retryable_error()` is invoked inside the retry handling path, but if a backend’s implementation raises (e.g., disposal/cleanup fails), it will mask the original backend exception and abort the retry loop. Consider wrapping the hook call in a `try/except` (best-effort cleanup + log) so retries still proceed on the original failure.
```suggestion
                        try:
                            self.on_backend_retryable_error(exc)
                        except Exception:
                            logger.exception(
                                "on_backend_retryable_error hook failed; continuing retry loop",
                            )
```

