```suggestion

@shared_task(
```

Using `self.tasks[name]` with a `try/except KeyError` means every `send_task()` call for an unregistered/remote task will raise and catch `NotRegistered` (a `KeyError` subclass). That can be a noticeable hot-path overhead for producer-only clients. Consider using `task_type = self.tasks.get(name)` (or `getattr(self.tasks, 'get', ...)`) to avoid exceptions in the common “not registered locally” case, while keeping the same fallback behavior.
```suggestion
            registry = self.tasks
            get = getattr(registry, 'get', None)
            if callable(get):
                task_type = get(name)
            else:
                try:
                    task_type = registry[name]
                except KeyError:
                    task_type = None
```

