review_comment:
If any `future.result()` raises, the exception will unwind out of the `with ThreadPoolExecutor(...)` block, and the executor context manager will still `shutdown(wait=True)` while other node shutdown tasks may be blocked (potentially reintroducing the “hang” this PR is trying to avoid on failure paths). Consider handling exceptions by canceling remaining futures (`cancel_futures=True`) and/or explicitly controlling executor shutdown so failures don’t wait on unrelated long-running shutdowns.
```suggestion
        executor = ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=max_threads)
        try:
            future_to_node = {
                executor.submit(_shutdown_single_node, node): node for node in nodes
            }
            for future in as_completed(future_to_node):
                try:
                    down_nodes = future.result()
                except Exception:
                    # Cancel remaining futures and avoid waiting on unrelated long-running shutdowns.
                    executor.shutdown(wait=False, cancel_futures=True)
                    raise
                if down_nodes:
                    for node in down_nodes:
                        maybe_call(on_down, node)
        finally:
            executor.shutdown(wait=True, cancel_futures=True)
```

