review_comment:
```suggestion

    def test_from_message_invalid_kwargs(self):
```

I don't think this is a better suggestion. Yes, it would work. But it would still need to resolve the app, and will be resolving the app to an incorrect app. Since we are only using the backend of the app for now, it wouldn't matter. But if we were to pass in the app instead of the backend, it would still leave us the ability to do anything else we want to do with the correct app if we wanted to do so in the future.

```python
    @classmethod
    def restore(cls, id, backend=None, app=None):
        """Restore previously saved group result."""
        app = app or (
            cls.app if not isinstance(cls.app, property) else current_app
        )
        backend = backend or app.backend
        return backend.restore_group(id)
```

