Prevent reauth from updating the existing entry with credentials from a different CatGenie account by validating the returned user_id matches the entry being reauthenticated (e.g., set unique_id from credentials and abort on mismatch, or otherwise block account changes). As written, reauth will accept any successful login and overwrite the entry token without checking it belongs to the same account.
```suggestion
                if reauth_entry.unique_id != credentials.user_id:
                    errors["base"] = "invalid_auth"
                else:
                    return self.async_update_reload_and_abort(
                        reauth_entry,
                        data={CONF_TOKEN: credentials.refresh_token},
                    )
```

Handle missing devices in coordinator data to avoid KeyError when the API returns an empty/changed device list. `device_data` uses direct dict indexing, but this integration’s coordinator can legitimately end up with `{}` (e.g., the empty-device-list refresh path), which would crash property access and break `available`/sensor updates; use a safe lookup and make entities unavailable (or remove them) when the device is absent.
```suggestion
    def device_data(self) -> Device | None:
        """Return the device data for this entity."""
        return self.coordinator.data.get(self._device_id)

    @property
    def available(self) -> bool:
        """Return True if entity is available."""
        device = self.device_data
        return super().available and device is not None and device.is_online
```

